Isn't it fairly uncontroversial that what speakers actually say in
their sentences is quite heavily determined by what things the
language makes easy to say and what things the language makes hard?

If that makes me a whorfian then I certainly am; I have long thought
that a the effectiveness of a logical language is proportional to
its ease of use, and that the goal of a logical language is to
translate logical formulas into something easier (that doesn't alter
the meaning).

